  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The manual does not say which BACnet card or transport (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP) is used.",
    "Instances are the '#' column of the manual's BACnet points list.",
    "Analog values are given 'in tenths' (one decimal place) per the manual.",
    "Eight integer points numbered 1001-1008 (Unit Status, CO2 In Zone, CO2 Outside, CO2 Differential, Heat Wheel Supply Pressure, Heat Wheel Exhaust Pressure, Air Flow Differential Pressure, Alarm Code) are typed 'INT', which is not a BACnet object type, so they are left out. The manual's tables decode Unit Status 0-8 and Alarm Code 1-17.",
    "BV 3 Alarm Active reads 0 = alarm, 1 = normal (inverted)."
  ],
